  "question": {
    "text": "The mean and the standard deviation (s.d.) of <math><mn>10</mn></math> observations are <math><mn>20</mn></math> and <math><mn>2</mn></math> respectively. Each of these <math><mn>10</mn></math> observations is multiplied by <math><mi>p</mi></math> and then reduced by <math><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo></math> where <math><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If the new mean and new s.d. become half of their original values, then <math><mi>q</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
